{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43698 - PROTEIN:5849",
  "verbalization": "Fluoranthene is implicated in the pathogenesis of A549 cells through a series of molecular interactions involving Ataxin-2, a protein that is targeted by multiple compounds, including (2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-2-[2-(3,4-dihydroxy-5-methoxyphenyl)-7-hydroxy-3-[(2R,3S,4R,5R,6S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxan-2-yl]oxychromenylium-5-yl]oxy-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxane-3,4,5-triol, (2E,4E)-N-isobutylundeca-2,4-dien-8,10-diynamide, and (-)-Duryne F. These compounds all share the common target of Ataxin-2, which is a key player in cellular processes that may contribute to the malignant transformation of A549 cells. The evidence suggests that Fluoranthene may act through a similar mechanism, potentially inhibiting Ataxin-2 and thereby affecting cellular functions in A549 cells. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting the same protein supports the hypothesis that Fluoranthene could exert a similar effect, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mechanism of action and its relevance to A549 cell behavior.",
